      en: "The Attapeu Sugar Factory, situated in the southern Attapeu Province, is a major agricultural processing facility established by the Hoang Anh Gia Lai (HAGL) Group from Vietnam. Surrounded by thousands of hectares of dedicated sugarcane plantations, the plant features industrial-scale crushing and refining technology capable of processing thousands of tonnes of cane per day. It produces refined sugar for domestic consumption and significant export volumes. The factory serves as an anchor for commercial agriculture in the region, providing steady employment and contracting opportunities for local farmers shifting away from subsistence agriculture."
